WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.911 --> 00:00:03.644
(cheerful piano music)

00:00:03.644 --> 00:00:07.193
- [Narrator] This is the
Panamanian golden frog.

00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:11.360
A frog so rare it may no
longer exist in the wild.

00:00:13.012 --> 00:00:16.980
Merely inches in size, this
frog's ornate skin is stunning.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.063
But also quite poisonous.

00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:23.300
The frog is covered in deadly toxins

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.050
to protect itself from predators.

00:00:27.561 --> 00:00:30.969
In the wild, it feasts on insects
that it finds near streams

00:00:30.969 --> 00:00:34.397
in the mountainous rain forests of Panama.

00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:36.889
But a combination of
deforestation, poaching,

00:00:36.889 --> 00:00:39.286
and a devastating fungal
disease laid waste

00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:41.468
to their population.

00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:45.918
But there is still hope
for this special amphibian,

00:00:45.918 --> 00:00:48.159
breeding in captivity has been successful.

00:00:48.159 --> 00:00:50.047
And continued efforts
are being made to protect

00:00:50.047 --> 00:00:52.297
and preserve their habitat.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.967
This is the Panamanian golden frog.

00:00:55.967 --> 00:00:59.217
(cheerful piano music)

